# ─── Environment template — SHAPE ONLY, never real values ────────────────────
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in real values. THIS file is committed,
# so it must never hold a secret.
#
# TRIMMED FROM THE PORTAL'S TEMPLATE. `asj-astro` carries ~40 variables — the
# Postgres connection, Netlify auth, Firebase service account, admin PINs,
# Grafana sinks. None of them exist in this repo: there is no database, no
# backend function, no push notification, no admin panel. Keeping them here
# would describe a system this repo is not, and an env template full of
# credentials that nothing reads is how a real token eventually gets committed
# to the wrong file. Only what the company profile page actually consults is
# listed below.

# ─── Supabase (client-side — PUBLIC_ prefix so Astro exposes it to the browser) ──
#
# The page itself renders without these. They exist because the copied shell
# (`src/lib/supabase.ts` via `src/store/userStore.ts`) still initialises a
# Supabase client, and a build without them prints
#   [Supabase] Missing PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL or PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY …
# and disables auth features. See README.md § "Yang MASIH terbawa" — removing
# that client entirely is the stage-2 job, and it would make these two lines
# unnecessary.
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# ─── Canonical origin — canonical link, hreflang, JSON-LD ────────────────────
#
# ⚠️ OPTIONAL BY DESIGN, AND EMPTY IS THE SAFE DEFAULT. With no `PUBLIC_SITE_URL`
# set, `src/lib/siteMeta.ts` emits NO canonical, NO hreflang alternates and NO
# JSON-LD at all. That is deliberate: a canonical pointing at the wrong origin is
# worse than no canonical, because it tells search engines to index a URL that
# does not serve this page.
#
# Set it to the origin that is actually DEPLOYING, once one is. Do not paste a
# host from memory — the portal's own origin has moved twice.
PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
